Petrklíč help is a youth, educational, community, and environmental non-profit operating since 2005 in Český Těšín, a town on the Czech-Polish border in Moravskoslezsky kraj (Silesia region). 
Petrklíč runs 8 distinct facilities and programmes: 
(1) A community house in Karviná with accommodation, training rooms, and a community garden; 
(2) Eco-farm PidiFarma Petrklíč in Kujavy for environmental education; 
(3) The Youth Regional Parliament engaging 120 young people from 12 towns; 
(4) Business Gate in Karviná — a social enterprise incubator with Silesian University; 
(5) A Forest Kindergarten and School in Ostravice; 
(6) Management of 20 Natura 2000 protected localities across Czechia and Poland; 
(7) Festivals including Earth Week, Tea Festival, and the “One World” human rights  film festival in Třinec; 
(8) Youth clubs, VR workshops, and art-mediation programmes.

The Institut de Formation aux Métiers Educatifs (IFME) and Europe House in Nîmes (south of France), is looking for 1 volunteer for a 11 months project:
- He/she  will have the opportunity to support the IFME's international team in transversal missions such as:
- canvassing and developing links with his/her country of origin in order to consolidate and perpetuate partnerships with universities and social work organisations ;
- promote incoming and outgoing student mobility
- Monitoring and updating the International page on the school's website ;
- Participating in applications for Erasmus +, the Occitanie region, the Franco-German Youth Office, etc.
- Helping to organise Erasmus days and International Social Work Day ;
- Run language and intercultural workshops ;
- Organising international events; 
- Working on intercultural projects;
- Assisting trainers in simulation workshops
- Drawing up a practical guide to student mobility depending on the destination

Venti di Scambio is an association of social promotion  founded in 2009 thanks to a call from the Puglia Region "Principi attivi". The objectives are:
- promote active citizenship of young people;
- promote solidarity, tolerance and understanding between different cultures;
- create a network both at a local level (schools, associations, administrations) and at an international level;
- give young people the opportunity to have a space where they can develop new skills and participate more in community life;
- create an increasingly large number of young people interested in European issues;
- raise young people's awareness of respect for the environment;
- increase youth employment and consequently local development and progress.
We have 1 more spot free and we are searching for a creative person who is ready to get out of comfort zone, developing some "crazy" art, manual but also online stuff with us!
https://mtv2019.wordpress.com/projects/venti-di-scambio-conversano/

Participate in various types of classes and cultural/language activities;
Be an active member of the school staff;
Assist foreign language teachers and teachers of the European Languages and Cultures elective;
Serve as an active ambassador and resource person for one’s own country and language;
Develop an understanding of European citizenship, values, solidarity, and human rights;
Organize two group activities for students, based on their interests and abilities (e.g., language, sports, cultural, or music clubs);
Show an interest in Breton culture, history, and traditions;
Improve one’s own knowledge of the French language.

The Brandenburgische Sportjugend is an independent working youth organisation in the ''Sports Federation Brandenburg''. Its members are children and teenagers, as well as their youth representatives who are organized in more than 2.500 sport-clubs. It counts more than 137 thousand members under the age of 27 and is the largest youth association in the state of Brandenburg. The project foresees to host 1 volunteer in the Organization´s Department of International Cooperation for 12 months. The Department imparts knowledge about planning, organization, implementation, finance and evaluation of international activities. 

Main tasks of the volunteer are: 
- support the co-workers of the Department in all their projects, 
- get acquainted with sport structures and EU programs and funding in international youth work; 
- support the planning, preparation and organization of international projects; 
- look after young people from abroad and international guests.

We are looking for motivated young people to join an international volunteer group project in Jēkabpils, Latvia for 19 days. This project focuses on creating meaningful connections between generations, supporting active ageing, and strengthening community spirit.

Main Activities

During the project, volunteers will:

Support the local Senior Day Centre by helping to diversify and enrich daily activities for seniors;
Organize creative workshops, games, cultural exchanges, movement activities, and informal social events;
Work together with local young people to prepare for the Jēkabpils City Festival;
Help create and facilitate activities where seniors can actively participate during the city celebrations;
Encourage inclusion, communication, and cooperation between generations.

Apprentis d'Auteuil is a Foundation of over 300 youth centres, welcoming, educating and supporting 40,000 young people in difficulty and their families, helping them build confidence and find their place professionally and personally.
The Sainte-Thérèse School Group supports middle and high school students and apprentices, with a focus on preventing school dropout, educational climate and inclusion.
The volunteer will take part in the educational life of the institution and support young people daily. They will:
- Welcome and integrate students;
- Support students during school activities;
- Organise educational, cultural or sporting activities;
- Foster intercultural exchanges;
- Participate in prevention initiatives;
- Support students' autonomy and self-confidence;
- Contribute to a positive school climate.

Based at 92-98 Boulevard Victor Hugo, Clichy-la-Garenne.

Ostello Monte Barro is looking for two volunteers who will be involved in environmental education activities. 
Tasks: 
- assist in hostel maintenance (indoor and outdoor) and logistics;
- check-in of the guests and administrative tasks;
- room preparation and cleaning;
- recycling and upcycling of materials for hostel use and decoration;
- provide guests with information like hiking paths and local area;
- assist in workshops for primary school students: facilitation and group management;
- design and implement didactic workshops on art, environment education, creative recycling;
- support in communication (social media, etc).
